<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>ErrorHandling on Bang Trinh - Developer</title><link>https://bangtrinh.github.io/my-blog/en/tags/errorhandling/</link><description>Recent content in ErrorHandling on Bang Trinh - Developer</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 20 Oct 2025 17:20:00 +0700</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://bangtrinh.github.io/my-blog/en/tags/errorhandling/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Java Exception Handling Tips</title><link>https://bangtrinh.github.io/my-blog/en/blogs/java-exception-handling-tips/</link><pubDate>Mon, 20 Oct 2025 17:20:00 +0700</pubDate><guid>https://bangtrinh.github.io/my-blog/en/blogs/java-exception-handling-tips/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Exception handling makes your code stable and easier to debug.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="example"&gt;Example&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-java" data-lang="java"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; result &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; 10 &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; 0;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;} &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt;(ArithmeticException e) {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; System.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;out&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;println&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Cannot divide by zero!&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;);
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;} &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;finally&lt;/span&gt; {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; System.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;out&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;println&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Always executed&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;);
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="tip"&gt;Tip&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;try-with-resources&lt;/code&gt; for AutoCloseable resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do not catch generic &lt;code&gt;Exception&lt;/code&gt; unless absolutely necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;N.B.&lt;/strong&gt; Good exception management keeps your application stable and easy to maintain.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>